  "final": {
    "agentMessage": "On CA DMV site searched **\"renew vehicle registration DMV office\"** - Service Advisor result:\n\n**Office renewal is the exception, not the normal process:**\n> **Option 1** Renew online. *In most cases, vehicle registration renewal is no longer processed at the DMV office and can be completed quickly and easily online, saving you time and postage.*\n- `Renew Online` button\n- If unable to use simple online app: `assisted virtual renewal service`\n\nOther non-office options listed:\n- **Option 2:** DMV Kiosks use touchscreen technology to guide you through renewing your registration. Kiosks are available inside select DMV offices and retail locations during regular business hours. `Find a kiosk near you.`\n- **Option 3:** Renew by mail to the address on your renewal letter.\n- **Option 4:** Renew by phone at **1-800-777-0133.**\n- **Option 5:** Vehicle registration renewals, duplicate sticker orders, and title transfers can be completed with DMV, or with DMV business partners and auto clubs. Business partners are authorized to charge a fee. `Find a Business Partner Location`\n\n**How to renew AT an office instead - Option 6:**\n> *There are cases that require renewal in person, such as eligibility, restrictions, etc. In these cases, you may schedule an appointment to renew at the DMV office.*\n- *I am ready to visit the office today.* \n  - Blue button: **Get in Line Now** - same-day line to save time\n- *I need an appointment in the future.*\n  - Link: **Make an appointment for registration renewal** - future appointment to save time on visit\n\nThat appointment / Get-in-Line-Now system is the stated way to save time on the office visit."
  },
